<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>(a) A spherical water tank at a school in Machakos has radius <m>{2}\,\text{m}</m>. The water surface is <m>{1.3}\,\text{m}</m> above the centre of the tank. Find the radius of the water surface, correct to 2 decimal places.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> m  </p><p>(b) Take <m>R = 6370\,\text{km}</m>. Find the radius of the parallel of latitude <m>{34}^\circ\,\mathrm{N}</m>, correct to the nearest km.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> km  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The centre of the tank, the centre of the water surface and a point on its edge form a right-angled triangle. The tank's radius <m>{2}\,\text{m}</m> is the hypotenuse and <m>{1.3}\,\text{m}</m> is one side, so</p><p><me>r^2 = {2}^2 - {1.3}^2 = {2.31}, \qquad r = {1.520} \approx {1.52}\,\text{m}.</me></p><p>(b) In the cross-section through the poles, the radius of the parallel is the side next to the angle of latitude in a right-angled triangle with hypotenuse <m>R</m>. A parallel is a small circle, radius <m>R\cos\varphi</m>, that shrinks to a point at the pole:</p><p><me>r = 6370 \cos {34}^\circ = {5281.0} \approx {5281}\,\text{km}.</me></p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>1.51986841536</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>5280.96933718</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>